`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"This course empowers faculty, instructional designers, and educational leaders to apply the 4D Framework to their own educational practice. Participants will learn to apply the 4D Framework to their own teaching practice, using AI as a thinking partner to enhance course design, create coherent learning materials, and develop authentic assessments while modeling responsible AI collaboration for their students."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"This course is the result of a long partnership between Anthropic and professors Rick Dakan from Ringling College of Art and Design and Joseph Feller from University College Cork. It builds on their experiences in training fellow educators and teaching the AI Fluency Framework to their students, and on feedback and questions that arose from our earlier course: AI Fluency: Framework & Foundations This course answers the question: how can I apply this framework to my personal teaching practice?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"The work was supported in part by the Higher Education Authority (Ireland) through the National Forum for the Enhancement of Teaching and Learning."}),`
